      "id": "nl590yb",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Time Period of the Vedic Age"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Vedic Period is broadly categorized into the Early Vedic Period (1500–1000 BCE) and Later Vedic Period (1000–500 BCE).",
        "The four Vedas comprise the Rigveda (oldest), Samaveda (music), Yajurveda (rituals), and Atharvaveda (charms and spells).",
        "Political organization evolved from tribal chiefdoms headed by a Rajan to territorial monarchies known as Janapadas.",
        "Democratic assemblies such as Sabha and Samiti served as crucial advisory councils to the king in the Early Vedic age.",
        "The economic base shifted from a pastoral and nomadic lifestyle to settled iron-age agriculture."
      ],
      "id": "fwhgxxz"
    },
